    "turn_text": "Well, until last week, I mean, the house is now moving basically to repeal the 2002 AUMF, which was action against Iraq, which I voted for because I believe the intelligence, I described my mistake in the book, and the intelligence was faulty. But anyway, to repeal that one, and then next up has to be a focus on this threadbare ancient quaint 2001 AUMF, which really no longer applies to the military missions we're engaged in. And my point is, last time I looked, we have a US Constitution. I'd like to keep it. It has three articles. One is Congress, which passes the laws. Two is the executive branch which carries out the laws, not makes the laws, and three is the federal judiciary. So, oops, where is article one? Where is Congress? Congress can't get things done because of toxic partisanship, but the other reason I can't get anything done is members don't want to own the consequences. And that is chicken.",
