    "turn_text": "Thank you. So anyway, yes and no, because we now have a homeland defense effort we didn't have before 9-11, although we are very, very susceptible to cyber attacks, especially ransomware. We have some defenses against that finally, but I'm just saying we are safer against physical attack airlines blowing up that we're safer against that. We're not safer against domestic terrorism and a very thoughtful strategy. Strategy is just released by the Biden administration on that and it is quite separate from our connection to foreign terrorism. A lot of these domestic attacks are not connected to cells operating in Afghanistan or pick a place, so there's that. But so, mixed on that record, in terms of internationally, again, I think that the dangers of nuclear war are present, but subsiding, we can talk about that. Again, I think our big threat at the moment, the perfect weapon, according to David Sanger of the New York times is cyber so we have that which wasn't there so and we have a broken Congress and we have a lot to repair in the world but we have a president who's set to do that and I think he does have a foreign and national security strategy first first guy and in five presidents",
