    "turn_text": "Yes and no. Let's start with the board. I mean, Greg Abbott, the governor of Texas, is clearly ambitious and maybe has 20, 24 stars in his eyes. I have no idea. But he's spending money to build the wall and says Mexico is going to help. I see no evidence of that. But maybe he'll use some federal money that he's getting instead of giving it to his people. He'll build more walls. So he's paying a big deal out of the border. It's a problem from hell, like many other problems. You can't just solve it by processing a silent claim faster because that draws more people. You have to solve it by starting at the push factors, which Biden is trying to do. And in fairness, Trump was trying to do this. There was once a conference in Miami early in the Trump administration with Vice President Pence and Luis Alberto Moreno, who was then",
