    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91042.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 61,
    "turn_text": "Biggest mistake. I think, you know, people will throw tomatoes at me, but I think he needs to give bipartisanship more of a chance, and I think he's dropped a few things. Shelley Moore Capito was meeting with him on infrastructure, Republican from West Virginia. Susan Collins was leading the meetings on the first COVID package, and I think he should have let those conversations go on longer. I'm not sure why he stopped them. I'm not saying that something isn't replacing them, but in both cases, I thought these are very capable people, and I'm not sure why he dropped those conversations as fast as he did.",
