    "turn_text": "And I think we can do that. I remember the day. I was in Congress in the 90s when we raised taxes and cut spending. In 1994, that was a career-risking move for Bill Clinton, who did get elected. And then in 1997, with Newt Gingrich, a speaker, I'm not shilling for Newt, all I mean, has become an acquaintance of mine since we both served there. But most of us voted for a balanced budget. And that was a big deal. That made America stronger. And it led to a period of real economic growth until 9-11. So I'm just saying that there is a strategic way to get to a better place. And again, I'm the one saying to you that Biden has strategy and has strategic thinkers in his government. So I can't answer that question just by itself. And I think they're thinking about this.",
