    "turn_text": "Well, I don't think a wealth tax makes a lot of sense, but I do think a fairer progressive income tax makes a lot of sense. And it was on the front pages of our papers a couple of weeks ago about the richest Americans pay no taxes. Well, oops, I'm not saying that's illegal, but I don't think that's smart. And I would rather see these proposals have been out there forever, a simpler progressive system where everybody pays some tax. I get it at the bottom. There needs to be some alternative tax or some kind of a reverse tax, which was started in the Clinton administration, which was quite successful if you make under the poverty rate. But I do think there's a way forward that smart people have already thought about that Biden could start to press that would probably leave the tax burden on those in the middle. I mean, he said he doesn't want to increase taxes for people earning under 400,000, which is a pretty hefty sum of money. But I think on a fair basis to simplify the tax code and to make all of us pay a fair share is the right way to go and we ought to do it right now.",
